  "definition": "Childhood schizophrenia is an outdated diagnostic term that was historically used for childhood mental disorders believed to be a type of schizophrenia. It appeared in earlier DSM versions but is no longer used as a separate concept, having been folded into the broader category of pervasive developmental disorders.",
